<details class="dev-tools">
  <summary>
    <i class="fa-solid fa-screwdriver-wrench"></i>
    <span>Developer tools</span>
    <span class="dev-tools-hint">For verifying server setup — not your hardware</span>
  </summary>

  <div class="dev-tools-body">

    <div class="dev-tools-warning">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i>
      <div>
        <strong>What this does <em>not</em> tell you.</strong>
        A successful test packet only confirms that ArckOne's server, your API key, and your schema all line up. It does <strong>not</strong> mean your actual hardware is sending data — that has to be verified by seeing real packets arrive in the listening indicator above.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-2"
         data-controller="test-packet"
         data-test-packet-url-value="<%= send_test_telemetry_workspace_path(@workspace) %>">
      <button type="button"
              class="btn-secondary text-xs flex items-center gap-2"
              data-test-packet-target="button"
              data-action="click->test-packet#send">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-flask-vial"></i>
        <span data-test-packet-target="label">Send a synthetic test packet</span>
      </button>
      <div data-test-packet-target="result" class="hidden text-xs"></div>
      <p class="text-[11px] text-[#9E9891] leading-relaxed">
        Sends one packet of dummy data, server-side. Useful while you're iterating on your schema or before your real hardware is ready.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</details>
